name: sim.getShapeColor
description: Retrieves the color of a shape
luaSynopsis: int result, list rgbData = sim.getShapeColor(int shapeHandle, string colorName, int colorComponent)
pythonSynopsis: int result, float[3] rgbData = sim.getShapeColor(int shapeHandle, string colorName, int colorComponent)
inputs:
1. shapeHandle: handle of the shape
2. colorName: name of a color. If a non-empty name is provided, a specific color component is retrieved (e.g. if a shape is a compound shape. If colorName is @compound, then rgb data for every component of a compound shape is returned)
3. colorComponent: color component
outputs:
1. result: 0 if the color name was not found in the shape, 1 otherwise
2. rgbData: red, green and blue components of the color (3 values), or the transparency value (1 value)
replacedBy:
